 "text": "Transformers\n\nThe European transformer market has experienced significant development over the last decade, driven by the growing demand for reliable and efficient power solutions in industrial, automation and critical infrastructure sectors. This equipment is essential for adapting electrical voltage levels and ensuring a stable, safe and high quality supply in environments where continuity of service is essential. \n\nWithin this sector, two main types of products stand out: toroidal transformers and conventional transformers, without forgetting the range of encapsulated transformers.\n\nToroidal transformers offer excellent energy efficiency, lower magnetic loss and a compact design that reduces electromagnetic interference, making them ideal for electronic, medical and precision applications. Conventional transformers, on the other hand, are characterized by their robustness, ease of maintenance and operational reliability, being indispensable in industrial and commercial installations that require constant performance under demanding conditions. \n\nQuality and regulatory compliance are decisive factors in the choice of a transformer, especially in Europe, where technical and environmental regulations demand high safety and performance standards.\n\nExplore subcategories\nConventional transformer\nConventional transformers in Europe The stability of the power supply in Europe depends to a large extent on the quality of its industrial components, especially conventional transformers. This equipment adapts electrical voltage levels to ensure safe and efficient use in sectors such as automation, electronics and heavy machinery. In demanding markets such as Europe, they must meet stringent technical standards to ensure performance and durability. Despite the advance of new technologies, conventional transformers remain essential for their robustness, ease of maintenance and operational reliability. In an environment where energy efficiency and durability are crucial, these transformers maintain their relevance thanks…\nLearn more\nToroidal transformers\nTorivac has more than thirty years of experience in the manufacture of all kinds of toroidal transformers. Toroidal transformers represent, like no other type, the ideal design of how a transformer should be. In fact, Faraday designed and wound the first transformer on a toroidal core. The toroidal cores manufactured by Torivac are built with grain oriented magnetic plate, with very low losses and high saturation induction and after being thermally treated, it allows reaching saturation values of up to 16,000 gauss. In the toroidal transformer, the magnetic flux is uniformly concentrated on the core and, due to the absence…\nLearn more\n\nTorivac-Products\n\n×\n\nProducts\n\nTransformers\n\n+\n\nConventional transformer\n\nToroidal transformers\n\nVoltage variators - Adjustable autotransformers\n\n+\n\nCustom manufacturing\n\nDesktop equipment\n\nDouble Variator\n\nRegulating accessories\n\nSingle Phase Inverters\n\nThree-phase drives\n\nVoltage stabilizers\n\n+\n\nAVS Series Stabilizers: electromechanical with servo motor\n\nBAVS Series: Electronics\n\nRheostats and coiled potentiometers\n\n+\n\nCeramic rheostats\n\nPotentiometers\n\nEncapsulated coils\n\n+\n\nRound\n\nSquares\n\nChokes | Inductances | Toroidal Reactances\n\n+\n\nNuclei\n\n+\n\nPortaled\n\n+\n\nled 10mm\n\nled 3mm\n\nled 5mm\n\nled 8mm\n\nSockets\n\n+\n\nHB4 socket\n\nHSR4 safety socket\n\nSafety socket HBS4\n\nsafety socket HR4\n\nControl buttons\n\n+\n\nArrow Discs\n\nArrow hoops\n\nBM series control buttons (Matte)\n\nBM Series Covers\n\nBO series control buttons (bright)\n\nBO Series control buttons with line\n\nBO series covers\n\nCasing covers\n\nEstators\n\nGraded covers\n\nGraduated discs\n\nResistors : Load banks\n\n+\n\nBoxed\n\nBraking resistors\n\nCemented\n\nGrounding resistors\n\nHelical\n\nLoad banks\n\nStarting resistors\n\nElectronic equipment\n\n+\n\nConverters\n\nDC power suppli